module Task.Internal exposing (Task)

{-| The type of a `Task`, in a module `core` does not expose
(`m1b-source.md` §SO11, after D233's `Bytes.Transient` and D240's
`Array.Transient`).

It was declared in `Platform`, which is the module close-out item 4 deletes, and
it cannot simply move into `Task`: `Platform.sendToApp` and `sendToSelf` answer
a `Task`, and `Task`'s own effect manager names `Platform.Router`, so the two
modules would import each other. A third module both can import is the same
answer the two transients gave to the same problem, and it is where the type
stays once `Platform` is gone.

A `Task` has no constructor that Geng can reach. The scheduler builds its nodes
in JavaScript, and until the `task_` group lands (D246) `Task`'s combinators are
the kernel's.

-}


{-| A description of something to do, which does nothing until it is run.
-}
type Task err ok
    = Task
